# Boot-time mixer defaults for the sun4i-codec card "Codec" (bd tsp-f3fm.220).
# Applied by /usr/lib/pocketforge/audio-defaults.sh (pocketforge-audio-defaults.service)
# as `amixer -c Codec cset name=<NAME> <VALUE>` for each `NAME=VALUE` line.
# A single value with no comma applies to every channel of a stereo control.
#
# Every NAME must exist in the open driver. tests/test-alsa-config.sh checks
# each NAME and VALUE against tests/fixtures/alsa/sun4i-codec-controls.*.tsv,
# which are taken from the driver source at each kernel pin.
#
# Speaker path on the TSP (sun50i-a133-pocketforge-tsp.dts &codec routing):
#   DAC -> Left/Right Mixer ("DAC Playback Switch") -> "Line Out Source
#   Playback Route" -> Line Out ("Line Out Playback Switch"/"Volume") ->
#   LINEOUT -> Speaker Amp (simple-audio-amplifier, enable PH6) -> Speaker
#   ("Speaker Switch" pin switch).
# Every gate is a register whose reset value is off, except the digital
# volume and the pin switch; all are set explicitly so boot state never depends
# on reset values or on what alsactl restored.
#
# Levels match the stock vendor boot values for the same registers
# (kernel-sunxi-4.9 pocketforge_tsp.dts codec node: digital_vol = <0x00>,
# lineout_vol = <0x1a>):
#   DAC Playback Volume 63 = DVOL register 0 (the control is inverted), 0 dB.
#   Line Out Playback Volume 26 = -7.5 dB (TLV: 2..31 is -43.5 dB + 1.5 dB/step).
# User-facing volume stays the softvol "Soft Volume Master" control from
# asound.conf, which this file does not touch.
DAC Playback Volume=63
DAC Playback Switch=on
DAC Reversed Playback Switch=off
Line Out Source Playback Route=Stereo
Line Out Playback Volume=26
Line Out Playback Switch=on
Speaker Switch=on
